id: pm-8s53lj
title: "Bare pm comments / pm notes reads keep the oldest page when output must be bounded, withholding the newest entries (GH-1605 fixed this for history only)"
description: "Measured on pm 2026.11.1 against this repository's tracker. When a bare read of an item's comments or notes has to be bounded, it returns the OLDEST page and withholds the newest entries:\n\n- pm comments pm-7zs0 --json (261 comments) returns 28 entries dated 2026-06-10..2026-06-30 with has_more: true and an output cursor. The newest entry (2026-11-01) is reachable only through --limit N (\"Return only latest n comments\") or by following about ten cursors.\n- pm notes pm-doxj --json returns 28 notes dated 2026-06-07..2026-07-10, while pm notes pm-doxj --limit 1 shows the newest note is from 2026-09-28.\n\nThis is the same defect GH-1605 (pm-gh1605) fixed for pm history: a default read should preserve the recent tail when it must truncate. The annotation surfaces did not get that fix. It has a real cost. While recording a release-health checkpoint, an agent verified its new comment with pm comments <id> --json | .comments[-1], saw a June entry, concluded the write had failed, and posted a duplicate that then had to be deleted with --delete. On long-lived living-map items, the newest evidence is exactly what the default view hides.\n\nScope: the default bounded selection for pm comments and pm notes (and pm learnings, if it shares the reader). Explicit --limit already selects the latest N."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,annotations,context-management,output-contract,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-11-01T11:19:29.712Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-01T12:19:04.795Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "A bare pm comments <id> and pm notes <id> read that must be bounded returns the newest entries (the recent tail) and reports the omitted older entries with a cursor that continues backwards; pm learnings follows the same rule; Regression test: an item with more annotations than the default bound returns the latest entry on a bare read in JSON and TOON; Command reference documents the bounded default for annotation reads"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: high
expected_result: A bare annotation read on a long-lived item always includes the most recent comment or note.
actual_result: pm comments pm-7zs0 --json returns 28 comments from June 2026 out of 261; the 2026-11-01 entry is withheld.
